    "Scouting Notes": "One of the most interesting pitchers in the system that we don't know much about. \n Throws around 91 94 or so as an 18 (soon to be 19) year old, with quite a bit of ASR.\n He throws a changeup that flashes plus.\n From what I've seen he throws a decent looking slider as well. \n He was very aggressively pushed to the ACL and unsurprisingly, he had some struggles his first year.\n I think that type of assignment clearly shows how the Brewers feel about him and they're showing it again by moving him to Low A the day before he turns 19\n Going to give him some time and see if he starts to catch up to the level he's pitching at, because I like the stuff quite a bit and his walk numbers have improved greatly from 2021 to 2022.",
